# ============================================================================
#  The AI layer is OPTIONAL. With no key at all the app still works end to end
#  on its built-in engines — it just answers more generically.
#
#  Put ONE of these in a file called .env (this file is the template).
#  Whichever key is present is the one that gets used.
# ============================================================================

# --- Google Gemini — has a free tier, no card needed to start ----------------
#   Key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   NOTE: on the FREE tier Google may use prompts and responses to improve its
#   products, and human reviewers may see them. This app only ever sends the
#   problem text, the word tapped, and the equation built — no names, no
#   account details. Decide for yourself whether that is fine for your child.
#   Paid tier prompts are not used for product improvement.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash      # Google retires these often; if you get a 404
#                                    # the server reads the replacement out of the
#                                    # error and switches, then tells you to pin it here

# --- Anthropic --------------------------------------------------------------
#   Billed per token from https://console.anthropic.com — this is SEPARATE
#   from a Claude Pro/Max subscription, which does not include API access.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5

# --- OpenAI -----------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Force one provider when several keys are present: anthropic | gemini | openai
# AI_PROVIDER=gemini

# --- Accounts (OPTIONAL) ----------------------------------------------------
#   Leave both blank and the app runs exactly as it does today: local profiles
#   on this device, no sign-in anywhere. The submission link must open into a
#   game, never a login form.
#
#   Both of these are PUBLIC values from your Supabase project settings.
#   There is deliberately no service_role key here and the server never needs
#   one: every query runs as the signed-in parent, so Postgres row level
#   security is what keeps one family's data away from another's.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

#   Google sign-in. Needs setting up in TWO places before this is any use — an
#   OAuth client in Google Cloud, and the provider enabled in Supabase — so it is
#   off by default. Worth having: it sends no email, so it is the way in when
#   Supabase's built-in sender hits its rate limit (2 an hour on the default).
# AUTH_GOOGLE=1
#
#   NOTE: with accounts on, turn OFF "Confirm email" in Supabase
#   (Authentication → Providers → Email). Left on, every new parent needs a
#   confirmation email — and the built-in sender allows two an hour.

PORT=5173
